-- Comms.lua : OUTLINE ONLY (RM-MPLUS, 2026-11-06). No code. Proposed, not decided. Open questions: ../README.md section 4.
-- One addon-message protocol for all parts. Prefix (16 characters max, warcraft.wiki.gg API_C_ChatInfo.SendAddonMessage): to choose.
-- Message kinds (proposed): HELLO (version, which parts I send), KICK, CC, CD (spell ID, start, duration), CDREADY, REQ (Requests.lua).
-- Channel: PARTY in a 5-player group (INSTANCE_CHAT for instance groups, per the wiki's chat type list); never GUILD or SAY.
-- Limits (wiki): 255 characters per message; 10 messages per prefix, then 1 per second; the server can change these at any time.
--   So: one message per spell use, coalesced; a queue that drops stale entries rather than sending late.
-- Lockdown: C_ChatInfo.InChatMessagingLockdown() (namespaces.md:827) and Enum.SendAddonMessageResult.AddOnMessageLockdown = 11
--   (enums.md:11741). While locked: send nothing, keep nothing queued past its use, and show "group sharing paused" once.
--   WHETHER IT IS LOCKED IN A KEYSTONE IS UNKNOWN: probe P1 first. The pattern to copy is XayaUI_Bonus/NotepadShare.lua:228-240 (own code).
-- Never sends a secret value (C_ChatInfo.SendAddonMessage has SecretArguments=NotAllowed, namespaces.md:844): check with issecretvalue
--   (as XayaUI/AuraList.lua:24 does) before building a message; a secret spell ID means "do not send", never a guess.
-- Received messages: name-checked against the group roster, version-checked, malformed ones ignored, nothing in them is run.
-- Q4: other addons' message formats are theirs (#290); not read or sent unless she decides otherwise.
